.TH LINDESK\-SESSION 1 "2026" "lindesk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lindesk\-session \- lindesk per-user session agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lindesk\-session
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-telemetry\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-standalone ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-adapters ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR FILTER ]
.br
.B lindesk\-session \-\-restore
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lindesk\-session
is the per-user half of lindesk. It runs unprivileged as a
.B systemd \-\-user
service
.RI ( lindesk\-session.service ,
part of
.IR graphical\-session.target )
and owns
.B org.lindesk.QoS1
on the session bus.
.PP
It tracks the foreground application and user input (built-in COSMIC and X11 adapters; the
GNOME Shell extension and the KWin script push over D-Bus), maps processes and app ids to
systemd user units, applies settings to those units through the user manager, hosts user
plugins and, with the optional
.B lindesk\-telemetry
package (the
.B telemetry
plugin), writes the user's telemetry lake. Without a
.BR lindeskd (8)
broker it runs the whole pipeline locally, limited to the user's own units.
.PP
All changes are runtime-only and restored on exit
.RB ( ExecStopPost=lindesk\-session\ \-\-restore ).
The agent re-reads its configuration and plugin directories on
.B SIGHUP
.RB ( "lindeskctl plugin reload" )
or on restart.
.PP
It runs
.B connected
when
.BR lindeskd (8)
is present (the broker's policy decisions are relayed to it) and
.B standalone
otherwise, switching as the broker comes and goes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Configuration file (default
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lindesk/lindesk.toml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Applied-state directory (default
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lindesk ).
.TP
.BI \-\-telemetry\-dir " DIR"
Telemetry lake (default
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/lindesk/telemetry )
for the
.B telemetry
plugin, when installed.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Observe only.
.TP
.B \-\-standalone
Never use the broker.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-adapters
Don't start the built-in desktop adapters.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " FILTER"
Log filter (else
.BR RUST_LOG ,
else
.BR info ).
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Revert every setting recorded in the state file, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH D-BUS
.B org.lindesk.QoS1
at
.IR /org/lindesk/QoS1 :
.BR SetForegroundProcess ,
.BR SetForegroundApp ,
.BR BeginInteraction ,
.BR EndInteraction ,
.B SetClass
(own processes only),
.BR ReportMetric ,
.BR Status ,
.B Explain
and the
.B LevelChanged
signal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lindesk/lindesk.toml
Configuration (default
.IR ~/.config/lindesk/lindesk.toml ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lindesk/rules.d/
Your classifier rules, consulted before the system's.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/lindesk/plugins/
User plugins (default
.IR ~/.local/share/lindesk/plugins ).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lindesk/state.json
Applied settings with their original values.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/lindesk/telemetry/
Your telemetry lake (default
.IR ~/.local/state/lindesk/telemetry ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lindeskctl (1),
.BR lindeskd (8),
.BR lindesk\-data (1)
